{
 "profile": "anime-director-v1",
 "about": "The bodies of coax/web/api/anime.c's two routes (proto/openagents/api/v1alpha1/anime.proto, profile api-routes; Protocol, GitHub #13250). \"routes\" and \"goldens\" have the form of proto/verse/api-routes-v1alpha1.json: each golden is a real answer of a running API, byte for byte, and \"from\" names the record in docs/verification/ it was copied from (runs of 2026-11-02 against a throwaway database; the live- records are a hosted model's answers to fixed test words). \"requests\" are real requests: the context- and fixture- records were written by the built CLI (openagents labs anime direct), the live- records by the API suite's harness. \"written\" holds bodies no run has recorded yet, exactly as the codec writes them today: the refusals the anime step of the API suite gives but no record kept, the refusals only a fault gives, and two replies of the animation director (POST /api/playtest/labs/anim/direct), which no suite calls; their \"request\" is the request the codec was given, and the direction in them is the unit check's, not a model's. Move a body from \"written\" to \"goldens\" when a suite run records it (API_CAPTURE; coax/web/api/tests/anime_direct.coax records every call). Checked by coax/web/api/anime-director-profile.coax, which reads and writes each body through the codecs (coax/web/api/anime-director-policy.coax, anime-route-policy.coax, metaverse-engine/anim/direction-select.coax) and holds its keys to its message; coax/web/api/routes-goldens.coax also takes this file.",
